VMM X64 SVM IMPORT MAP

This directory contains the active AMD SVM backend built by
sys/dev/virtual/vmm/Makefile on x86_64.

ACTIVE BUILD INPUTS

  vmm_svm.c
  vmm_svm_backend.c
  vmm_svm_entry.S

SOURCE MAP

  vmm_svm.c
    Source: sys/dev/virtual/nvmm/x86/nvmm_x86_svm.c
    Role: AMD SVM machine setup, VMCB state, VMRUN loop, and VMEXIT decode.
    Differences: VMM object names and public x64 ABI spellings are applied directly.
    The NVMM ioctl/cache/config layer is replaced by the VMM backend interface and the
    caller-owned vmm_cpustate/vmm_cpuexit ABI.

  vmm_svm_entry.S
    Source: sys/dev/virtual/nvmm/x86/nvmm_x86_svmfunc.S
    Role: low-level VMRUN entry wrapper.
    Differences: exported symbols use the vmm_svm_ prefix.

  vmm_svm_x86defs.h
    Source: sys/dev/virtual/nvmm/x86/nvmm_x86.h, lines 356 through 716.
    Role: CPUID, CR, MSR, XCR, EFER, and SVM feature-bit definitions.
    Differences: extracted into a VMM-private header; no NVMM state, ioctl,
    capability, or configuration structures are included.

  vmm_svm_os.h
    References: sys/dev/virtual/nvmm/nvmm_os.h,
                sys/dev/virtual/nvmm/nvmm_dragonfly.c,
                sys/dev/virtual/nvmm/x86/nvmm_x86_internal.h.
    Role: DragonFly allocation, pmap, token, CPU, FPU, debug-register, and
    IPI glue used by the imported SVM implementation.
    Differences: binds those operations to VMM ownership and M_VMM; it has no
    dependency on nvmm.ko.

VMM-SPECIFIC FILES

  vmm_svm.h
    Private AMD SVM backend declarations matching struct vmm_backend_ops.

  vmm_svm_backend.c
    VMM backend probe and linker-set registration.

REVIEW BOUNDARY

The active backend has no include of sys/dev/virtual/nvmm and no unresolved
nvmm_* or M_NVMM module symbol.  The only imported implementation files are
the SVM C loop, the VMRUN assembly wrapper, and the documented architecture
definition subset above.  Old unbuilt VMM SVM prototype files were removed.
